I think that just pulling out the words or concepts would not do the trick.  We 
need to be able to cover what the child *says*, not merely the words s/he uses 
individually, especially since the words turn out in context to have a variety 
of meanings, often far from the base.  I haven't look at the db, but if it does 
not include conversations -- and fairly long ones at that -- it will ultimately 
not be satisfactory (that is, it wi;; leave it open for critics to say we have 
not made our case.)




